# Legacy .html URLs from the pre-restructure site. These paths no longer
# correspond to real files (content now lives under clean-URL directories),
# so without an explicit rule Cloudflare Pages was falling back to serving
# the homepage's index.html at each of these URLs — with its canonical tag
# pointing back to the homepage. That created duplicate-content pages at
# stale URLs. 301 them straight to the correct current page instead.
/whats-included.html   /whats-included/   301
/pricing.html           /pricing/           301
/landing-pages.html     /landing-pages/     301
/about.html             /about/             301
/faq.html               /faq/               301
/guides.html            /guides/            301

# Catch-all: any URL that doesn't match a real file or one of the specific
# redirects above would otherwise fall through to Cloudflare's generic 404
# page. Send visitors to the homepage instead. This must stay LAST in this
# file — Cloudflare Pages evaluates _redirects rules top to bottom and uses
# the first match, so anything more specific above still takes priority.
# 302 (temporary), not 301: these are broken/unknown links, not pages that
# permanently moved to the homepage, so we don't want that signal cached
# long-term by browsers or credited as a permanent move by search engines.
/*   /   302
